# Routes

`routes.ts` is the list of who can open a path. `proxy.ts` reads it.

- `publicRoutes` — reachable signed out.
- `authRoutes` — sign-in, register, and auth errors. Signed-in users redirect to `DEFAULT_LOGIN_REDIRECT`.
- `apiAuthPrefix` — NextAuth handlers.

Add a page to the matching list when it should be public or auth-only. Do not add a one-off signed-out check inside the page.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — new public page is declared once
export const publicRoutes = ['/about', '/terms', '/support', '/privacy', '/auth/verify'];
```
